      <activity id="f7f23cc3-ccdd-55da-83c8-5b07c6a6f702" activityNameId="24dec386-4176-5690-ae5d-bdfc4f320fb7" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Natural gas, production TT, at long-distance pipeline</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Natural gas, production TT, at long-distance pipeline
In 2023 0% of the imported Trinidadian and Tobagan natural gas to JP was imported by pipeline and 100% as LNG. An average distance of 0 km is estimated for the pipeline export from Trinidad and Tobago, of which are 0 km offshore pipeline. The estimated shipping distance for LNG are 16400 km. The net calorific value of natural is 36.0 MJ/Nm³. UUID=6189fab3-1ae3-3c62-a807-1b5374662a97
This dataset describes the transport needed for an average export of Trinidadian and Tobagan natural gas. Gas losses and emissions during seasonal storage are included.
Location: The data for storage emissions are based on global data. The amount of gas stored is a rough estimate based on European data. The average weighted transport distance is based on the trade movements 2019.
Technology: The distance is an European average based on the European long-distance pipeline network and LNG shipping routes.
Time period: Transport modes investigated for 2023.
Production volume: not known
Sampling: Literature.
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_6189fab3-1ae3-3c62-a807-1b5374662a97.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
